  <metadata>
    <id>hold</id>
    <version>0.0.0</version>
    <title>Hold</title>
    <authors>Darryl Wright</authors>
    <owners>Darryl Wright</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/punkscience/hold</projectUrl>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/punkscience/hold</projectSourceUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/punkscience/hold/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/punkscience/hold/releases</releaseNotes>
    <tags>keep-awake caffeine sleep tray</tags>
    <summary>Tray app that keeps Windows awake while you are away.</summary>
    <description>Hold is a small Windows tray app that stops the computer from sleeping while it is on.

* Open eye: Hold is on. Closed eye: Hold is off. Left-click the icon to switch.
* Right-click for "Keep display on" and Quit.
* Starts at login for every user on the machine.
* While on, and once the user has been idle for 50 seconds, Hold sends a synthetic zero-distance mouse move about once a minute. The pointer does not move, but Windows counts it as input, so apps that watch for idle time see the user as present.
* On battery, Hold turns itself off when the charge drops below 10%, and turns back on when power is reconnected.

Hold makes no network calls and stores one per-user registry value.</description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
